{"reply":"In Chapter 3, the Dodo announces, “_Everybody_ has won, and all must have prizes.” When they ask who will give them, he points to Alice: “Why, _she_, of course,”

The thimble comes from that reversal: Alice is treated as the prize-giver, distributes what she has, and then is ceremonially given back something that was already hers. The Dodo presents it as an elegant thimble, and everyone behaves as though the ceremony has made it a meaningful reward, while Alice finds the whole thing absurd (Chapter 3, “A Caucus-Race and a Long Tale”).

That helps illuminate your lunches without making the situations identical. The awkwardness may lie in the mismatch between recognition and reciprocity: being thanked acknowledges your effort, but it does not necessarily return the deposit, the planning, or the risk in a form that eases your load. It can feel less like receiving something new than having your own contribution ceremonially handed back to you. Does that fit what feels odd—the thanks themselves, or the fact that the practical burden remains yours?","evidence_uses":[{"source_kind":"book_corpus","evidence_id":"pg11-v01b38ea4-ch03-ln0553-0587","source_location":"Chapter 3 — A Caucus-Race and a Long Tale, source lines 553-587","supported_claims":["In Chapter 3, the Dodo announces, “_Everybody_ has won, and all must have prizes.”","When they ask who will give them, he points to Alice: “Why, _she_, of course,”"],"exact_quote":"“_Everybody_ has won, and all must have prizes.”"},{"source_kind":"book_corpus","evidence_id":"pg11-v01b38ea4-ch03-ln0578-0617","source_location":"Chapter 3 — A Caucus-Race and a Long Tale, source lines 578-617","supported_claims":["The thimble comes from that reversal: Alice is treated as the prize-giver, distributes what she has, and then is ceremonially given back something that was already hers.","The Dodo presents it as an elegant thimble, and everyone behaves as though the ceremony has made it a meaningful reward, while Alice finds the whole thing absurd (Chapter 3, “A Caucus-Race and a Long Tale”)."],"exact_quote":null}],"memory":{"kind":"no_memory_candidate","reason_code":"automatic_capture_disabled"}}

